    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are positioned for a high-ceiling outing today, headlined by **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (76.34) and **Jackson Merrill** (75.10). **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** benefits from a favorable matchup against a starter with a high 4.80 xERA, while **Jackson Merrill** is a priority start due to his ability to exploit a slow opposing pitcher delivery\u2014a critical advantage in our pursuit of stolen bases. **Jacob Wilson** (74.07) also commands an elite score due to a prime leadoff spot and a soft matchup against Mitch Bratt (7.04 xERA). These three anchors provide the foundation for our offensive efficiency, capitalizing on clear SP skill advantages.\n\nSecondary value today is driven by park and platoon dynamics. **Drake Baldwin** (68.94) and **Josh Jung** (64.32) are high-floor plays, with **Drake Baldwin** receiving a significant boost from his leadoff placement and favorable hitting environment. While **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** and **Nasim Nunez** face a neutral matchup against Freeland, they remain active due to the high park factor at Coors. Conversely, **Andy Pages** (48.81) faces the toughest test of the day against a sub-3.00 xERA arm and a difficult defensive catcher, keeping his score in the marginal range. **Gunnar Henderson** (56.76) also takes a slight dip due to a platoon disadvantage against Tolle, but his raw talent keeps him in the utility slot over the bench.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision involved **Coby Mayo** (55.80), who narrowly missed the cut behind the projected efficiency of **Heliot Ramos** and **Cole Carrigg**. While **Coby Mayo** benefits from positive park factors, the optimizer preferred the superior matchup context surrounding our outfield contingent. Finally, managers should monitor the \"Lineup Pending\" status for several players, specifically **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Nasim Nunez**, **Wade Meckler**, and **Cole Carrigg**. Any shifts in batting order\u2014particularly for **Jacob Wils